<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner in UK oil deal with Elf.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner in UK oil deal with Elf.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kvaerner ASA said on Wednesday it had been awarded a contract by Elf Exploration UK Plc for operations and maintenance of oil and gas platforms on the British continental shelf.</p>
<p>The five-year deal is worth 220 million crowns in the first year, according to a statement on the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>&quot;Kvaerner and Elf will work together to fully exploit the platforms Piper B, Saltire A and Claymore and the Elgin/Franklin field,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>Kvaerner will carry out maintenance, engineering and modification, in addition to support functions within supplies and safety.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
